course: dictionary
lesson: 890
title: One word, many meanings: birth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word birth has three main meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one the writer means. «Some children are adopted: they join a family that did not give birth to them.» Here give birth to means the time when a baby comes out of its mother, so that is the meaning to choose.
explain: The meaning can change even when the word looks the same. «The birth of a new nation» is not about a baby at all. Here birth means the beginning of something. Ask yourself: does the sentence still make sense if I swap in "beginning"? If it does, you have found the right meaning.
explain: Some words sit in set phrases. «By birth» means by the family or place you were born into, so «Irish by birth» tells you where a person's family or place of birth is. Phrases like date of birth, birth certificate and birthplace are worth learning as chunks, because they always go together.
fact: Birth is a noun: a thing or event you can name.
fact: Birth means the time when a baby or young animal comes out of its mother's body and starts living in the world.
fact: Birth can also mean the beginning of something, as in «the birth of» a country.
fact: «By birth» means by the family or place you were born into.
fact: Useful phrases: give birth to, at birth, date of birth, birth certificate, birthplace, birth weight.
exercise: «Some children are adopted: they join a family that did not give birth to them.» What does give birth to mean here? | *The time a baby comes out of its mother | To buy a new family home | To grow taller than your parents | To hold a party for someone
exercise: «The birth of the internet changed how people talk.» What does birth mean here? | A baby coming out of its mother | *The beginning of something | A family name | A date written on a form
exercise: «She is Irish by birth.» What does by birth mean? | By a boat or a plane | By accident, with no plan | *By the family or place you were born into | By the time you are ten
test: Which phrase means the day you were born, as written on a form? | *Date of birth | Birth certificate | Birth weight | Birthplace
test: What is the name for how heavy a baby is when it is born? | Birthday | Birthplace | *Birth weight | Birth certificate
exam: «...so that it does not drown during the birth» is from a sentence about a whale calf. What does birth mean here? | *The time a young animal comes out of its mother's body | A party for the calf | The date written on its certificate | The beginning of a new whale family
